Sval: each embed shim keeps its own placeholders and observer

Every embed shim in a frame shares one copy of smartblock_embeds_helper.js:
the shims run in one content script sandbox, and executing the file again
for the next shim throws on the redeclared const, which lib/shims.js
swallows. Its placeholders and observer were that copy's globals, so
unblocking one shim disconnected another's observer and restored every
shim's embeds while its own observer kept watching, and that observer gave
its embed its placeholder back.

